{"kind":"request","text":"Self-hosting note, draft 4: the single-node drain case and the waker's latency (item 5 of a6847815).\n\nThe SeaweedFS evaluation of 27 October (notes/implementation/2026-10-27-seaweedfs-local-bucket.md, section 3) found two things that the self-hosting note does not cover. A celld node with no live peer never seals its stop: every SIGTERM logged shutdown_handoff_stalled, no `node-log close: sealed epoch` line, and the node record kept \"draining\": true with no `log` object. Section 4.7 calls any end without the sealed line an unknown drain. And a timed rule on a cold cell fired 20.2 s late, because celld's waker scans every 60 s by default. Section 6 still says alarms were never seen firing.\n\nOne planner head on planner/selfhost-drain-20261108 changes notes/2026-10-19-self-hosting-on-celld.md only: 4.7 gains the case of a node with no live peer, checked by its node record alone under celld v0.6.3's guarantees; section 5's drain row, section 9's H4 witnesses and decision 9 follow; section 6 replaces the alarm bullet with the observed firing and the waker bound; the status line, section 12 and the sources record draft 4. No code, no Mac kit change, no deployment. Order afdebb86 lists this as a planner phase-1 item.","body":{"conditions":"One planner head changing only notes/2026-10-19-self-hosting-on-celld.md: every celld claim cites the v0.6.3 docs or the SeaweedFS evaluation record; the drain rule with a live peer stays as draft 3 states it; prose lines at most 79 characters; check-doc-links 0 broken; check-notes 0 warnings; check-section-citations 0 broken; one checker review at the exact head before landing; no deployment.","target_head":"f1ec237cfe9cb66c5fef74cdd54889d1c77d5bd6","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}